0017:     Extend each control pixel perpendicular to the full bars, marking every bar hit with a 3x3 contact marker.
0018: 
0019:     Input structure
0020:     - The background is the dominant color.
0021:     - Exactly one foreground color forms one or more complete parallel rows or complete parallel columns.
0022:     - The other foreground color appears as isolated control pixels off those bars.
0023: 
0024:     Rule
0025:     - For each control pixel, cast rays in both directions perpendicular to the bars.
0026:     - Stop each ray at the first bar cell it reaches and color the control-to-hit segment with the control color.
0027:     - After all rays are drawn, stamp a 3x3 block of the bar color centered on each hit, restoring the center to the control color.
0028:     - Directions with no bar before the grid edge emit nothing.
0029: 
0030:     Key insight
0031:     - The only complete rows or columns identify the bars and their orientation; the contact markers are layered after the rays.
0032:     """
0033:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0034:     H, W = g.shape
0035:     bg = get_bg(g)
0036:     colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
0037: 
0038:     bar_candidates: list[tuple[int, list[int], list[int]]] = []
0039:     for color in colors:
0040:         rows, cols = _complete_lines(g, color)
0041:         if rows or cols:
0042:             bar_candidates.append((color, rows, cols))
